cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  bonesim: a virtual UWB microwave imaging study for long-bone
  fracture detection
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Amalnath
    family-names: K P
repository-code: https://github.com/amalnathkp13-boop/bone-fracture-rf-sensing
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-08-25
keywords:
  - microwave imaging
  - ultra-wideband
  - bone fracture
  - FDTD
  - gprMax
  - openEMS
  - Vivaldi antenna
abstract: >-
  A complete, purely computational study of non-invasive long-bone fracture
  detection by ultra-wideband microwave imaging over 3-11 GHz. Tissue
  dielectrics, electromagnetic propagation, antenna design, the imaging chain
  and the statistical analysis are all modelled with open-source software; no
  hardware was built. Across 192 full-wave acquisitions from eight simulated
  specimens, fractured and intact limbs separate by 40.8 dB with no overlap.
  The study also demonstrates experimentally that a saturated area-under-curve
  statistic conceals the loss of more than half that margin when usable
  bandwidth is restricted.
